commit 22f215eb3e7d9814cb3e29f42856e56bb57e60ed
Author: BrilliantWasp <brilliantwasp@proton.me>
Date:   Sun Nov 8 20:35:58 2026 +0000

    psi: preserve common fields when matching case values (#2078)
    
    A match on a record with case fields could lose its common fields and
    field constraints, or evaluate a saved producer again. This preserves
    the same value through checking, borrowed calls and execution. It also
    updates the affected patterns to the current syntax. The original
    programs, inputs and expected results are preserved.
    
    [The host program and rejection
    control](https://github.com/CathedralOS/Omega/actions/runs/42517029267)
    passed: native and Psi both exited 0 with exact I/O, and the invalid
    borrow rejected. [Admission checks and eight existing interpreter
    tests](https://github.com/CathedralOS/Omega/actions/runs/42518845745)
    passed on `810ed6d0`. The host compiler is `7531da20`. Later edits only
    narrow Rust helper visibility, move an unchanged test block and record
    existing fixture measurements; independent review confirmed that the
    successful executions still apply. Required PR checks validate the final
    source.
    
    Two programs covering [case-field
    stores](https://github.com/CathedralOS/Omega/tree/810ed6d0b0f760f0c1172608f8432e9b020450a8/tests/omega/pass/structs/case_field_type_store_shapes)
    and [composed payload
    reads](https://github.com/CathedralOS/Omega/tree/810ed6d0b0f760f0c1172608f8432e9b020450a8/tests/omega/pass/structs/runtime_composed_case_payload_reads_exit)
    passed checking but were refused by native borrow validation in the
    earlier run. Their status on the current candidate is unverified, and
    this PR does not claim to fix them. They remain outside this landing and
    are not counted as successes.
    
    [Earlier
    execution](https://github.com/CathedralOS/Omega/actions/runs/42463003477)
    produced native/Psi agreement for 23 of 25 programs. [Earlier source
    checking](https://github.com/CathedralOS/Omega/actions/runs/42460884915)
    checked 28 of 29 positive programs and all 18 intended invalid controls.
    These are historical results from optimized compiler `9af3eb51`, not
    executions of the current integrated compiler.
    
    [Three supplemental diagnostic-pin mismatches also occur on
    main](https://github.com/CathedralOS/Omega/actions/runs/42445244680).
    Those programs reject, but the three unchanged pins remain unsatisfied
    and are excluded from passing counts.
    
    The parent scalar migration remains open. Claim:
    `0f80365597144c0a93cb4136e1c4e7d0`.
    
    The provenance below covers a shared coordinating-session window, not an
    exclusive cost for this PR.
    
